        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "What is the value of $\\frac{2}{3}\\int_{1}^{4}\\frac{4{log}_{4}\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=\\log_{4}\\left(\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)\\right).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}\\,\u27f9\\,\\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}\\int_{1}^{4}\\frac{4{log}_{4}\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{8}{3}\\int_{1}^{4}{log}_{4}\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{8}{3}\\int_{0}^{1}u\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}4\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{8 \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}{3}\\int_{0}^{1}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\left(4\\operatorname{ln}4\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}\\right)|_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\left(2\\operatorname{ln}4\\cdot (1-0)\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\left(2\\operatorname{ln}4\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\left(4\\operatorname{ln}2\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
